      "id": "good-strategy-bad-strategy-s013-p01017",
      "source_en": "1. Wernher von Braun to the Vice President of the United States, 20 April 1961, NASA Historical Reference Collection, NASA Headquarters, Washington, DC. 2. The first better photograph of the surface was taken by Ranger 7 in 1964, snapped at an altitude of about one thousand feet before it smashed into the surface. The photo did little to settle the hard-soft-sharp debate, and it showed only objects that were larger than about three feet.",
